      "title": "A warm cache carries the load",
      "body": [
        "Within minutes the popular trails are all cached and the <span class=\"term\">hit ratio</span> settles at 93%. Only 7 requests in 100 reach the database.",
        "Median latency drops from 95 ms to 16 ms and database CPU from 80% to 14%. Popularity is uneven — a few trails get most views — which is exactly why a small cache can absorb most traffic."
      ],
      "callout": {
        "kind": "insight",
        "text": "Every point of hit ratio matters: going from 90% to 95% hits halves the load on the database."
      },
