    {
      "short": "Stale",
      "chapter": "problem",
      "title": "The cache doesn't know the trail closed",
      "body": [
        "Each entry has a <span class=\"term\">TTL</span> (time to live) of one hour, after which it's dropped and re-read. At 10:05 a ranger closes Eagle Ridge after a rockslide. The database is updated — but the cache keeps serving “OPEN” until 10:58.",
        "For most data a little staleness is fine. For a closed trail it isn't. Shorter TTLs help but cost hit ratio; the real fix is to tell the cache when data changes."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "+ Ranger closes the trail",
        "~ Cache still serves the old answer"
      ],
