    {
      "short": "Invalidate",
      "chapter": "solution",
      "title": "Write, then delete the key",
      "body": [
        "Now every update goes through the app, which writes the database and then <b>deletes</b> the cache entry — <span class=\"term\">invalidation</span>. The next reader misses, reads “CLOSED” from the database, and refills the cache.",
        "Deleting is safer than writing the new value into the cache: if two updates race, a delete can't leave the wrong one behind. Keep the TTL as a safety net for any update path you forget."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "+ Update deletes the cached key",
        "~ Hikers see CLOSED within a second"
      ],
