    {
      "short": "Eviction",
      "chapter": "technique",
      "title": "When the cache is full",
      "body": [
        "The cache has 4 GB; Ridgeline has 60 GB of trail data. When it's full, something must go. Most caches use <span class=\"term\">LRU</span> — evict the least recently used entry — so popular trails stay and forgotten ones leave.",
        "Because a small slice of trails gets most views, caching just 7% of the data still yields about 90% hits. Doubling the cache would add only a few points."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "~ Cache full: least recently used entries evicted"
      ],
