      "short": "Calm herd",
      "chapter": "solution",
      "title": "One rebuild, everyone waits for it",
      "body": [
        "<span class=\"term\">Request coalescing</span>: on a miss, the first request takes a short lock and rebuilds the entry; the others wait briefly for its result, or get the slightly old value meanwhile (<span class=\"term\">stale-while-revalidate</span>). One query instead of hundreds.",
        "Add <b>jitter</b> to TTLs — say 55–65 minutes instead of exactly 60 — so entries filled together don't all expire together."
      ],
